# Intent: the link looks on the default face, drawn from shapes (rebuild of the old 111, 112 and 113 on the current base; owner 2026-11-13; docs/design/feature-gap-2026-11-16.md Train 1 item 5). No font, image or mint skin part is added: the glyphs are rectangles and one line. (1) LINK SCREEN (111): the boot cover gets a glyph slot above its text: the Wi-Fi bars at 1.5 times the old size, cycling while it says "Connecting to Wi-Fi..." or "Connecting to Home..."; the slashed bars for "Wi-Fi setup needed", which now shows the hotspot name and the address on two lines (they went to the speech bubble, which is hidden while captions are off, so nobody could read them), also when setup is asked for after the boot; and the slash with a key for "Waiting for Home to approve me". The glyphs exist only while a look shows, so a linked unit holds none. (2) OFFLINE LOOK (112): after the first face, a small strip in the top-left corner replaces the speech-bubble "Offline" (invisible with captions off): after 3 s without the hub the bars cycle with no words; after 45 s (patch 143's delay, unchanged) the slashed bars and "Offline" appear with the existing dim amber ring; the first hello removes the strip and the ring. (3) WAITING FOR APPROVAL (113): Home accepts the websocket and closes it before its hello when it has not approved the unit; the hello wait now ends at once on that close, and two such connects in a row show the key look (full screen before the first face, the corner strip "Waiting for approval" and a cyan ring blink after it, the steady amber steps aside) and send one "ws_refused" event; the first hello clears it. hal_bridge gets link_look(0 up, 1 connecting, 2 offline, 3 refused); offline_indicator(bool) now calls it and offline_indicator_refresh() does nothing. NOT taken from 111 to 113 (and why): the muted "offline" face palette and the eyes 5 px lower (the face colour belongs to the saved face config, F01, and a firmware-only transient palette risks being saved; the strip, the words and the ring already say offline); "Can't reach Home" riding on the strip (the existing speech-bubble message stays); the mint skin parts (not in this base). The link text is English only, like the boot text it replaces.
# Placement: unit (the link state runs on the robot, with or without a host)
# Upstream: main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc, stackchan.cc, hal_bridge.h of the M5Stack StackChan firmware and main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc, websocket_protocol.h of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT)
# Check after a flash: power on with Wi-Fi off: the screen shows cycling bars and "Connecting to Wi-Fi..."; with no saved network it shows slashed bars, "Wi-Fi setup needed", the hotspot name and the address, and the ring blinks cyan. Stop the hub after the face is up: after 3 s the bars cycle in the top-left corner, after 45 s the strip says "Offline" and the ring turns dim amber; start the hub: both go. Use a hub that has not approved the unit: after two quick closes the key look shows and a ws_refused event reaches the host log; approve it and the look clears on the first hello.
